SUMMARY:Upstairs at Helium: Collin Chamberlin
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 10 W. Georgia St.\, Portland
DESCRIPTION:Collin Chamberlin is one of the best up and coming comedians to
 uring. Originally from Pittsburgh\, Collin now resides in New York City\, b
 ut his Steel Town roots are clear on stage.\n\nHis clean\, quick\, and conv
 ersational style is fun for anyone. It’s like hearing a story from an old
  friend.\n\nCollin has been featured on major platforms including\; Don’t
  Tell Comedy\, DryBar\, and CBS’ Comics Unleashed.\n\nHe’s been seen on
  the Are You Garbage Podcast and tours with some of the biggest acts in the
  country\, including Are You Garbage and Jessica Kirson.\n\nCollin is also 
 the host of the popular outdoor series\, Up Camp. A true homage to his home
 town. You can stream Collin’s first special “Hello\, It’s Me” on Yo
 uTube!\n\nPLEASE NOTE: our Upstairs showroom is 21+ and is NOT wheelchair a
 ccessible.\n\nManagement reserves the right to prevent customers from enter
 ing the facility who they deem disruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nM
